# Walkthrough: Clean Planner Implementation

I have implemented a unified planner architecture that gracefully merges academic data (Canvas assignments, NUSMods timetable) with personal tasks.

## Key Accomplishments

### 1. Unified Schema ([planner.py](file:///Users/oli/Desktop/CraftCanvas/backend/schemas/planner.py))
Created a [PlannerItem](file:///Users/oli/Desktop/CraftCanvas/backend/schemas/planner.py#12-37) schema that abstracts different event types into a consistent format for the frontend.
- [planner.py](file:///Users/oli/Desktop/CraftCanvas/backend/schemas/planner.py)

### 2. Aggregation Service ([planner_service.py](file:///Users/oli/Desktop/CraftCanvas/backend/services/planner_service.py))
Developed a service that polls multiple data models and combines them into a single chronological stream.
- [planner_service.py](file:///Users/oli/Desktop/CraftCanvas/backend/services/planner_service.py)

### 3. Clean API Router ([planner.py](file:///Users/oli/Desktop/CraftCanvas/backend/schemas/planner.py))
Exposed a single endpoint `/api/v1/planner/grid` to simplify frontend state management.
- [planner.py](file:///Users/oli/Desktop/CraftCanvas/backend/routers/planner.py)

### 4. Application Integration
Registered the new planner module in the main entry point.
- [main.py](file:///Users/oli/Desktop/CraftCanvas/backend/main.py#L86)
- [main.py](file:///Users/oli/Desktop/CraftCanvas/backend/main.py#L130)

## How to Test
1. Restart the backend server.
2. Query `GET /api/v1/planner/grid?start_date=2026-03-14&end_date=2026-03-21`.
3. Verify that the response includes a mix of `task` and `assignment` types with unified fields.
